**How Parse recognises a new file:**

`Parse` repeatedly calls `findFileMarker`, which scans for a line that starts with `"-- "` and ends with `" --"`. The text between those delimiters (with surrounding whitespace stripped) is the file name.

**The function that checks a single line:** `isMarker` (line 117). It verifies that the data begins with `"-- "` and ends with `" --"` on the same line (up to the next `\n`), then returns the trimmed filename.

```go
// isMarker checks whether data begins with a file marker line.
// If so, it returns the name from the line and the data after the line.
// Otherwise it returns name == "" with an unspecified after.
func isMarker(data []byte) (name string, after []byte) {
    if !bytes.HasPrefix(data, marker) {
        return "", nil
    }
    // ... extract up to \n ...
    if !(bytes.HasSuffix(data, markerEnd) && len(data) >= len(marker)+len(markerEnd)) {
        return "", nil
    }
    return strings.TrimSpace(string(data[len(marker) : len(data)-len(markerEnd)])), after
}
```

